UNSQZ13 goes the usual USQ programs one better....

1) it allows for the source file to be deleted after unsqueezing
2) it allows unsqueezing across drive/user areas

UNSQZ uses ZCPR2-style syntax to designate drive/user areas


EXAMPLES:

	..>unsqz13 b7:*.* a5: $e
	   (unsqueezes all squeezed files from B user 7, places the
	    output files into A user 5 and deletes the squeezed
	    source files. Note that regardless of the actual input
	    filename specified, t2 always becomes "Q"!)
	..>unsqz13 *.*
	   (same as if you'd say, "unsqz13 *.?Q?")
	..>unsqz13 *.* $q
	   (query unsqueeze)

Note that version 1.30 is safe to use with large files now.

REASSEMBLY:
	should reassembly be necessary, it must be assembled with M80
	and linked with either L80 or LINK (preferred). The link file
	sequence MUST BE WILDEX,USQBASE,SYSLIB!

	WILDEX.REL is a product of ESKAY Software Service
	USQBASE.REL is (c) Dave Rand
	SYSLIB.REL is (c) Richard L. Conn
